== 1.9 Chapter 1 Practice Drill — 30 Questions

30 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 33 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [The part of a neurone that conducts impulses away from the cell body is the],
  [nucleus],
  [myelin sheath],
  [axon],
  [dendrite]
)

#mcq(2, [The junction between two neurones is called a],
  [ganglion],
  [synapse],
  [reflex arc],
  [node of Ranvier]
)

#mcq(3, [An impulse crosses a synapse by means of],
  [movement of the nucleus],
  [osmosis of water],
  [a chemical transmitter],
  [electrical conduction through the myelin]
)

#mcq(4, [The myelin sheath speeds up conduction because it],
  [contains the nucleus],
  [absorbs the impulse],
  [insulates the axon so the impulse jumps from node to node],
  [produces the transmitter]
)

#mcq(5, [Which of the following is *not* a component of a reflex arc?],
  [Hormone],
  [Sensory neurone],
  [Receptor],
  [Effector]
)

#mcq(6, [The gap between two neurones is called the],
  [myelin gap],
  [dendron],
  [synaptic cleft],
  [node of Ranvier]
)

#mcq(7, [A neurone that carries impulses from a receptor to the central nervous system is a],
  [motor neurone],
  [hormonal neurone],
  [sensory neurone],
  [relay neurone]
)

#mcq(8, [The nervous system and the endocrine system differ in that the nervous system],
  [is faster and shorter-acting],
  [uses the blood as its route],
  [acts only on glands],
  [is slower and longer-acting]
)

#mcq(9, [A stimulus is best defined as],
  [the gap between two neurones],
  [the response of a muscle],
  [a gland that secretes a hormone],
  [a change in the environment that an organism can detect]
)

#mcq(10, [Which sequence correctly describes a reflex action?],
  [Effector → motor neurone → CNS → sensory neurone → receptor],
  [Receptor → sensory neurone → CNS → motor neurone → effector],
  [Receptor → motor neurone → CNS → sensory neurone → effector],
  [CNS → receptor → effector → sensory neurone]
)

#mcq(11, [The cell body of a sensory neurone is found in the],
  [synaptic cleft],
  [cerebrum],
  [ventral horn of the spinal cord],
  [dorsal root ganglion]
)

#mcq(12, [An effector is],
  [the gap between two neurones],
  [a muscle or a gland that carries out the response],
  [a receptor in the skin],
  [a neurone in the spinal cord]
)

#mcq(13, [The all-or-none law means that],
  [a stronger stimulus always gives a bigger impulse],
  [impulses travel in both directions],
  [a stimulus either produces a full impulse or none at all],
  [impulses can cross any gap]
)

#mcq(14, [Transmission at a synapse is one-way because],
  [transmitter is stored only in the presynaptic knob and receptors only on the postsynaptic membrane],
  [the cleft is too wide],
  [the nucleus is in the way],
  [the myelin blocks the return]
)

#mcq(15, [The refractory period is the],
  [time taken to make myelin],
  [resting potential of the cell],
  [gap between two neurones],
  [short time after an impulse when the membrane cannot be stimulated again]
)

#mcq(16, [Motor neurones are also called],
  [sensory neurones],
  [efferent neurones],
  [relay neurones],
  [afferent neurones]
)

#mcq(17, [Which structure increases the speed of conduction along an axon?],
  [Myelin sheath],
  [Synaptic vesicle],
  [Nucleus],
  [Dendrite]
)

#mcq(18, [A reflex action is described as automatic because],
  [it happens only when you are asleep],
  [it is slower than a voluntary action],
  [it involves no neurones],
  [it does not need a decision by the brain]
)

#mcq(19, [The dendrites of a neurone function to],
  [produce myelin],
  [carry impulses away from the cell body],
  [secrete hormones],
  [receive impulses and carry them towards the cell body]
)

#mcq(20, [Which of these is a reflex action?],
  [Standing up from a chair],
  [Deciding to read a book],
  [Writing your name],
  [Blinking when something flies at the eye]
)

#mcq(21, [A drug that blocks the enzyme which destroys the transmitter at a synapse will cause],
  [continuous stimulation of the postsynaptic membrane],
  [the myelin to disappear],
  [no change at all],
  [the impulse to travel backwards]
)

#mcq(22, [The direction of an impulse along a neurone is],
  [axon → cell body → dendrites],
  [dendrites → cell body → axon → axon terminals],
  [cell body → dendrites → axon],
  [terminals → axon → cell body]
)

#mcq(23, [A relay neurone is found],
  [only in the skin],
  [only in the heart],
  [in the myelin sheath],
  [entirely within the central nervous system]
)

#mcq(24, [Which part of a neurone contains the nucleus?],
  [Axon terminal],
  [Myelin sheath],
  [Cell body],
  [Axon]
)

#mcq(25, [The nervous system is NOT responsible for],
  [deciding to move a hand],
  [the slow growth of a child over years],
  [a knee-jerk response],
  [detecting a change in temperature]
)

#mcq(26, [A stimulus produces no response in a neurone until it reaches the],
  [node of Ranvier],
  [synaptic cleft],
  [axon terminal],
  [threshold]
)

#mcq(27, [Nodes of Ranvier are],
  [swellings in the cell body],
  [the gap at a synapse],
  [gaps in the myelin sheath],
  [the ends of dendrites]
)

#mcq(28, [If a sensory neurone is cut, the animal will],
  [grow a new brain],
  [not detect the stimulus at all],
  [respond without any stimulus],
  [detect it more strongly]
)

#mcq(29, [Which statement about reflex actions is correct?],
  [They involve only the cerebrum],
  [They are controlled by hormones],
  [They are slow and always conscious],
  [They are rapid, automatic and protective]
)

#mcq(30, [Comparing nervous and hormonal control, hormones],
  [reach every cell but act only on cells with the right receptor],
  [act only on one named muscle],
  [travel along neurones],
  [act within milliseconds]
)

